 * Hinglish: Hindi written in the English alphabet, the way people actually type it. Tech words everyone
 * already says in English (server, port, RAM, Java, address, backup, world) stay in English.
 * Each key is the exact English text the app shows (see I18n.kt); `{name}` marks a value filled in at
 * run time and must appear in the translation too. Text that reads the same in both languages is left out
 * (HinglishTest keeps a list of those). HinglishTest checks that nothing is missing and nothing is left over.
 * The wording matches the desktop app's Hinglish file.
 */
